ation robustness rank aggregation from pairwise comparisons\",\n400\t    \"Elo rating system relation to Bradley-Terry sports game outcomes\",\n401\t    \"statistical inference uncertainty ranking from pairwise comparisons confidence intervals bootstrap\",\n402\t    \"Chatbot Arena open platform for evaluating LLMs by human preference\",\n403\t    \"Judging LLM-as-a-judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena human pairwise judgments\",\n404\t    \"Understanding black-box predictions via influence functions\",\n405\t    \"Cook's distance case deletion diagnostics one-step approximation logistic regression\",\n406\t    \"adversarial vote manipulation of LLM arena leaderboard rankings\",\n407\t    \"robustness of rankings from pairwise comparisons to adversarial or corrupted comparisons\"\n408\t  ],\n409\t  \"reference_query_plan\": {\n410\t    \"architectural_shifts\": [],\n411\t    \"benchmarks\": [\n412\t      \"Chatbot Arena human preference battles (55k / 140k)\",\n413\t      \"MT-Bench human expert judgments\"\n414\t    ],\n415\t    \"central_topic\": \"Citation gaps in a paper on minimal removal sets (verified by exact Bradley-Terry refit) that flip adjacent-pair rankings of pairwise-comparison leaderboards: the Chatbot Arena / MT-Bench data and platforms, influence-function and case-deletion diagnostics behind the first-order removal ranking, and manipulation or corruption of crowd-vote and pairwise-comparison rankings.\",\n416\t    \"comparators\": [\n417\t      \"influence-only row removal (B2 comparator)\",\n418\t      \"adversarial manipulation and vote rigging of crowd-vote leaderboards\",\n419\t      \"robustness of pairwise-comparison rankings to corrupted comparisons\"\n420\t    ],\n421\t    \"core_methods\": [\n422\t      \"first-order (one-step Newton) influence of deleting a row on the Bradley-Terry score gap, with leave-one-out leverage correction\",\n423\t      \"case-deletion diagnostics (Cook's distance style) for logistic-type likelihoods\"\n424\t   