3\t      \"central_topic\": \"Minimal removal sets (verified by exact Bradley-Terry refit) that flip pairwise-comparison leaderboard rankings, and how the budget differs between crowd-vote (Chatbot Arena), expert/LLM-judge (MT-Bench) and sports (NBA Elo) comparison data.\",\n484\t      \"comparators\": [\n485\t        \"random-removal baseline\",\n486\t        \"permuted/shuffled-outcome control\",\n487\t        \"influence-function and AMIP-style dropping-data robustness metrics\",\n488\t        \"vote-rigging and adversarial manipulation of crowdsourced leaderboards\",\n489\t        \"bootstrap/confidence-interval based ranking uncertainty\"\n490\t      ],\n491\t      \"core_methods\": [\n492\t        \"Bradley-Terry maximum-likelihood fitting on pairwise outcome counts\",\n493\t        \"first-order influence / approximate maximum influence perturbation for data-dropping robustness\",\n494\t        \"greedy removal search with exact-refit verification, prefix bisection and swap polish\",\n495\t        \"cell-aggregated (pair-count) weighted refits with relaxed removal search\",\n496\t        \"stationarity-LP over target ratings for minimal removal sets\"\n497\t      ],\n498\t      \"forbidden_query_patterns\": [\n499\t        \"generic optimization or benchmarking surveys\",\n500\t        \"scientific method or paper-writing phrasing\",\n501\t        \"chronology of cycles, attempts or search history\",\n502\t        \"internal score names such as combined_score or rubric\",\n503\t        \"titles, authors or results of the withheld published paper on this research question, or pages citing it\",\n504\t        \"unrelated LLM architecture or training queries\"\n505\t      ],\n506\t      \"queries\": [\n507\t        {\n508\t          \"category\": \"core_method\",\n509\t          \"query\": \"Bradley-Terry model paired comparisons maximum likelihood estimation ranking\",\n510\t          \"rationale\": \"Defines the scoring model refit exactly in every flip-budget