 success indicator true, diagnostics unverified); paper.tex lines for the qualification subsection and Discussion (iii). || fix=Say only that the sealed evaluation completed and was recorded as qualified with a true success indicator. Report the control results as separate observations from the episode evidence. Delete the statements that qualified certifies controls passing, and add that the qualification gate criteria are not recorded in the evidence.\nAUDIT_FINDING: id=evaluator-internals-unsupported || section=Problem Setup 3.4 and 3.5, Supplement Controls and Algorithmic specification and Data provenance || claim=B3 deletes rows where the upper participant beat another participant, ordered by opponent rating. The permutation control is non-vacuous only within 90% of expected moved fraction and spread at most half. The evaluator's acceptance test is theta_hi<theta_lo with no margin. Held-out content hashes are tested for overlap and the evaluation aborts on any overlap; tables are checked by checksum. Cross-table copy rescales row indices. || issue=These describe evaluator internals (comparator construction, control thresholds, acceptance rule, abort-on-overlap and checksum behaviour, copy-control mechanics). The only inspectable source is the candidate and baseline program under source_evidence/downstream, and no evaluator source or spec is staged. claims_grounding.json has no claim for these details. The abort-on-overlap statement also sits awkwardly beside the recorded removal of 2 overlap rows and the 652 kept prompt-only overlaps. || evidence=source_evidence/downstream contains only baseline and program (program.py, datasets_offline.py, program_spec.toml); claims_grounding.json covers budgets, scores and control outcomes but not comparator or control construction; derived/task_meta/final_meta.json shows 2 rows removed and 652 prompt-only overlaps kept. || fix=Remove or explicitly mark as not independently verifiable the evaluator-implementation specifics: t